ImportC supports `__try`, `__except`, and `__finally`

MSVC's structured exception handling statements are now supported in
ImportC, lowered to D's own try/catch/finally:

-------
__try {
    riskyCall();
} __except (filter) {
    handleIt();
}
-------

The filter expression is an ordinary C expression; `1`
(`EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER`) runs the handler, anything else rethrows,
since `EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_EXECUTION` has no D equivalent. `_exception_code()`
and `_exception_info()` are not supported, since the hardware-exception
information they need isn't preserved by the time a fault reaches D.

(On win64, a real exception through `__except` crashes LDC's SEH/unwind
lowering; DMD's own backend is unaffected.)
